  <h1>Terms</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: 26 November 2026</p>

  <p>These terms cover Frame Multiplier, the free Figma plugin where you pay to release frames, and our
    setup service for it. By releasing frames you agree to them. Monochrome Systems makes the plugin
    and runs the service.</p>

  <h2>Previews are free</h2>

  <p>The plugin is free to install and use. Multiply makes a low-res, watermarked JPEG preview of each
    frame's layout, as often as you like, at no cost. Previews are for checking the rollout; they are
    not working artwork.</p>

  <h2>What a release buys</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>The frames in the order.</strong> Releasing turns the previews of the frames you chose
      into working frames, laid out from your masters and delivered on a new page in your file. The
      page you work on keeps its previews.</li>
    <li><strong>Four rounds.</strong> A release is four deliveries of the same frames: the release itself
      and three more. Each round is delivered on its own new page, so you can change the masters, check
      the previews and deliver again.</li>
    <li><strong>40 days.</strong> Rounds 2 to 4 must be delivered within 40 days of payment, and the
      plugin shows the last day. Round 1 has no time limit.</li>
    <li><strong>Per frame.</strong> A round is counted for each frame delivered. A duplicate of a frame
      is a new frame and is not covered. A copy of the file shares the original's rounds; it doesn't
      get its own.</li>
    <li><strong>Delivered pages are yours.</strong> They stay in your file whatever happens to the order
      later, and you can use them as you like.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We can add rounds or days to an order, for example when something went wrong on our side. The
    plugin shows them the next time it is opened.</p>

  <h2>Price</h2>

  <p>A$1 a frame, with an A$9 minimum per order, in Australian dollars. The price is shown on the
    Release button before you order, and any tax is shown at checkout. There is no subscription and
    no credit is kept: you pay for each order.</p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>

  <p>Payment is taken by Lemon Squeezy, which is the merchant of record for the sale: it charges you,
    handles any tax and sends the receipt. Its
    <a href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/buyer-terms">buyer terms</a> apply to the payment as well as
    these. Paying outside Figma is how this plugin works; Figma does not take or hold the payment.</p>

  <h2>Delivering</h2>

  <p>Each delivery is counted by our order server, so delivering needs an internet connection. If you
    are offline, one round can be delivered and is counted when you are back online; the next waits.
    If a delivery fails to lay out, its round is kept and the next Deliver tries again. Undoing a
    delivery in Figma does not give the round back.</p>
  <p>Frame Multiplier lays out each frame from your masters. Always check the delivered frames before
    you send them to print or publish them.</p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>

  <p>If a release doesn't work and we can't fix it, email us within 30 days of payment with the order
    number on your receipt and we will refund it in full. A refunded order ends its remaining rounds;
    pages already delivered stay in your file.</p>
  <p>Nothing in these terms limits your rights under the Australian Consumer Law, or the consumer laws
    of your own country.</p>

  <h2>Setup service</h2>

  <p>If you <a href="/help/frame-multiplier/request/">ask us to set up a file</a>, setup is free. You
    see every size as a preview before you decide. If you release the frames, the release costs A$1 a
    frame with an A$49 minimum, and covers the same four rounds in 40 days. If you don't release,
    you pay nothing. With edit access we work in your file; remove our access when the job is done.</p>

  <h2>Your work</h2>

  <p>Your designs, images and text stay yours. We use your file only to do what you ask, and the
    plugin sends none of your artwork anywhere (see <a href="/help/frame-multiplier/privacy/">Privacy</a>).
    You need the rights to the artwork you lay out with the plugin.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>

  <p>The plugin runs inside Figma, so it depends on Figma and on Figma's terms. We may change or stop
    the plugin or the service; rounds already paid for are honoured within their 40 days. Except where
    the law says otherwise, our liability for an order is limited to what you paid for it.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>If these terms change, this page changes first, with a new date at the top. The terms on the day
    you paid apply to that order.</p>

